---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="The Data Platform — Case Study"
  description="Owned customer and order data infrastructure across 200+ merchants on five e-commerce platforms; webhook freshness moved from days-late batch data to sub-minute."
>
  <article style="padding: 52px 0;">
    <nav style="margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <a href="/case-studies" style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">← Back to case studies</a>
    </nav>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 24px;">
      <h1 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: var(--fs-32); font-weight: 600; margin: 0; flex: 1;">The Data Platform</h1>
      <button onclick="navigator.clipboard.writeText(window.location.href); this.textContent='Copied!'; setTimeout(() => this.textContent='Copy link', 2000);" style="padding: 8px 16px; border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: transparent; cursor: pointer; font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); white-space: nowrap; border-radius: 3px; transition: all 0.2s ease;" onmouseenter="this.style.borderColor='var(--accent)'" onmouseleave="this.style.borderColor='var(--rule)'">Copy link</button>
    </div>

    <p style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-2); margin-bottom: 32px; max-width: 65ch;">I owned the rebuild of customer and order data infrastructure across 200+ merchants on five commerce platforms. Webhook freshness moved from days-late batch data to sub-minute.</p>

    <div style="display: flex; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-bottom: 32px;">
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">days → sub-minute</span>
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">200+ merchants</span>
      <span style="background: var(--accent-wash); color: var(--accent); padding: 8px 12px; border-radius: 3px; font-size: 13px;">3-month migration · rollback path designed</span>
    </div>

    <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-3); margin-bottom: 40px;">Node.js · MySQL · Debezium · Google Pub/Sub · Datastream · MongoDB · BigQuery · ClickHouse · Redis · GKE</p>

    <!-- My Role -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 24px;">My Role</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">What I personally owned</h3>
        <div style="display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 65ch;">
          <div><strong>Architecture and technical direction</strong> — designed ingestion, CDC, and multi-layer serving architecture</div>
          <div><strong>CDC strategy</strong> — chose Debezium path, landing-layer design for reversibility</div>
          <div><strong>Migration strategy</strong> — planned and executed store-by-store cutover across 200+ merchants</div>
          <div><strong>Production rollout</strong> — owned monitoring, alerting, and incident response across about five years of platform ownership</div>
          <div><strong>Core implementation</strong> — architected and directed the CDC pipeline, landing store, and warehouse consolidation; team (4→7 engineers) built and maintained</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">What the team delivered</h3>
        <div style="display: grid; gap: 12px; max-width: 65ch;">
          <div><strong>Platform team grew from 4 to 7 engineers</strong> — directly managed the team (1:1s, code review, hiring decisions) alongside architecture and deployment strategy</div>
          <div><strong>Team delivery</strong> — continuous production monitoring, reliability work, and incremental optimization</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Context -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Context</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;">ConvertCart serves 200+ e-commerce merchants across five platforms (Shopify, BigCommerce, WooCommerce, Magento 1, Magento 2). Customer data, orders, click-tracking, and loyalty data all flow through separate systems with no unified schema. Downstream products (recommendations, segmentation, attribution) need to access this data, but latency and availability are unpredictable.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Problem -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Problem</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 24px;">Data arrives days late. Commerce webhooks provide near-real-time events, but custom platform integrations require full data downloads every 6 hours. Click-tracking and loyalty data are even slower. Downstream products can't build real-time features. Reporting is expensive because queries have to reprocess data constantly. New products need to build custom integrations instead of tapping a shared stream.</p>

      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 32px; margin-top: 24px;">
        <div style="padding: 20px; background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px;">
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">BEFORE</div>
          <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">6+ hour batch delays</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Custom integrations per product</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Expensive BigQuery reporting</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink);">No unified data model</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div style="padding: 20px; background: var(--panel); border-radius: 4px;">
          <div style="font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">WHY IT MATTERED</div>
          <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Real-time recommendations impossible</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Segmentation used stale data</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 8px;">Attribution couldn't link orders to blocks</li>
            <li style="font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink);">Every new feature required engineering</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Architecture -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Architecture</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 24px;">Consolidates four source systems (commerce, click-tracking, loyalty, CRM) into a raw MySQL landing store, preserving original schema. Debezium streams changes via Google Pub/Sub. Downstream layer fans out to three specialized stores: MongoDB for point lookups (serving), ClickHouse for analytics, BigQuery for historical data.</p>

      <!-- Architecture SVG Diagram -->
      <svg viewBox="0 0 640 480" style="max-width: 65ch; width: 100%; margin-bottom: 24px; display: block;" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <defs>
          <style>
            .arch-box { fill: var(--panel); stroke: var(--rule-2); stroke-width: 1.5; }
            .arch-label { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; fill: var(--ink); }
            .arch-label-small { font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 10px; fill: var(--ink-2); }
            .arch-arrow { stroke: var(--ink-3); stroke-width: 2; fill: none; marker-end: url(#arrowhead); }
            .arch-accent { fill: var(--accent); }
          </style>
          <marker id="arrowhead" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="9" refY="3" orient="auto">
            <polygon points="0 0, 10 3, 0 6" fill="var(--ink-3)" />
          </marker>
        </defs>

        <!-- Sources: Commerce, Click-tracking, Loyalty, CRM -->
        <rect class="arch-box" x="20" y="20" width="140" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="90" y="50" text-anchor="middle">Commerce</text>

        <rect class="arch-box" x="180" y="20" width="140" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="250" y="50" text-anchor="middle">Click-tracking</text>

        <rect class="arch-box" x="340" y="20" width="140" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="410" y="50" text-anchor="middle">Loyalty</text>

        <rect class="arch-box" x="500" y="20" width="120" height="50" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="560" y="50" text-anchor="middle">CRM</text>

        <!-- Arrows from sources -->
        <line class="arch-arrow" x1="90" y1="70" x2="120" y2="110"/>
        <line class="arch-arrow" x1="250" y1="70" x2="200" y2="110"/>
        <line class="arch-arrow" x1="410" y1="70" x2="380" y2="110"/>
        <line class="arch-arrow" x1="560" y1="70" x2="450" y2="110"/>

        <!-- MySQL Landing Layer -->
        <rect class="arch-box" x="60" y="110" width="440" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="290" y="138" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">MySQL Landing Layer</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="290" y="155" text-anchor="middle">(raw, per-source schemas, reversible landing layer)</text>

        <!-- Arrow to CDC -->
        <line class="arch-arrow" x1="290" y1="170" x2="290" y2="210"/>

        <!-- Debezium CDC + Pub/Sub -->
        <rect class="arch-box" x="80" y="210" width="420" height="60" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="290" y="238" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Debezium CDC → Google Pub/Sub</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="290" y="255" text-anchor="middle">(replay boundary, per-tenant isolation)</text>

        <!-- Arrows to serving layer -->
        <line class="arch-arrow" x1="160" y1="270" x2="100" y2="310"/>
        <line class="arch-arrow" x1="290" y1="270" x2="290" y2="310"/>
        <line class="arch-arrow" x1="420" y1="270" x2="480" y2="310"/>

        <!-- Serving Layer: MongoDB, ClickHouse, BigQuery -->
        <rect class="arch-box" x="20" y="310" width="140" height="70" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="90" y="335" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">MongoDB</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="90" y="355" text-anchor="middle">(serving)</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="90" y="370" text-anchor="middle">point lookups</text>

        <rect class="arch-box" x="200" y="310" width="140" height="70" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="270" y="335" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">ClickHouse</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="270" y="355" text-anchor="middle">(analytics)</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="270" y="370" text-anchor="middle">aggregation</text>

        <rect class="arch-box" x="380" y="310" width="140" height="70" rx="4"/>
        <text class="arch-label" x="450" y="335" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">BigQuery</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="450" y="355" text-anchor="middle">(historical)</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="450" y="370" text-anchor="middle">audit trail</text>

        <!-- Ownership & SLO annotations -->
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="290" y="190" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent); font-size: 9px;">Platform team owns</text>
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="290" y="280" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent); font-size: 9px;">5min alert, 15min page</text>

        <!-- Consumption callout -->
        <text class="arch-label-small" x="290" y="430" text-anchor="middle" style="fill: var(--accent);">← Recommendations, Segmentation, Attribution, Reporting</text>
      </svg>

      <p style="font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 65ch;">New sources plug into the landing layer. New consumers subscribe to Pub/Sub. No custom integrations required. Platform team owns the landing layer and CDC; 5-minute latency alerts, 15-minute on-call page threshold.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Key Decisions -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Key Decisions</h2>
      <ol style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>Landed raw instead of normalizing at ingest</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Costs: five schemas instead of one. Benefit: reversibility. Wrong normalization at ingest means multi-service migration. Wrong view is a redefinition away from correction.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>CDC from landing store, not sources</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Costs: one more moving part. Benefit: CDC from a consolidated landing layer with replay and validation boundaries.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 20px;">
          <strong>Two replication paths (Datastream + Debezium)</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Started with managed Datastream, gradually earned our way to pure Debezium. Avoided speculative engineering while managing risk.</span>
        </li>
        <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">
          <strong>Table-per-client multiplies operational surface</strong><br/>
          <span style="color: var(--ink-2);">Thousands of tables, migrations run across all. Accepted because shared-table contention is worse and less visible than operational overhead.</span>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- Execution -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Execution</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Migration Strategy</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Store-by-store cutover because the data layer sits under every product. Bad cutover breaks all of them simultaneously. Slow but safe.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Backfill & Validation</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Dual-wrote to old and new landing layers for 2 weeks. Hourly validation compared row counts, key distributions, timestamp ranges, and checksums across migrated tables before each cutover.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Rollback Strategy</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Kept old pipeline running for 30 days after cutover. If anything broke, could revert to old data. Never had to use it, but reduced risk psychologically and operationally.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">Monitoring & Alerting</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0;">Added metrics for data freshness (time from source to landing to serving), lag per store, checkpoint latency. Alerts on 5-minute latency deviation. Page on-call for >15 min delays.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin: 32px 0; padding: 24px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 4px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">The production incident that changed the design</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 12px;">When Debezium attempted to snapshot the 50M-row landing store: the query consumed 60% CPU and blocked production writes. Unacceptable. We stopped the rollout immediately.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>What we did:</strong> leveraged the existing Datastream snapshot to seed the baseline, then transitioned tables to Debezium CDC incrementally. This became our dual-replication strategy.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;"><strong>The lesson:</strong> don't optimize for architectural purity when production is at risk. Reversibility and operational safety trump elegance.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin: 32px 0; padding: 24px; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 4px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">The consumer crashes that weren't a memory leak</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 12px;">As client volume grew, Pub/Sub-consuming services began crashing intermittently. Looked like a code-level memory leak — local testing showed nothing, because the failure only surfaced under production traffic volume and real message throughput.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch; margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>What we did:</strong> traced it to Kubernetes pod memory limits, not application code. Consumers were pulling messages as fast as Pub/Sub delivered them with no regard for available headroom. The pod's memory ceiling (not the app) was what triggered the crash. Fixed by adding backpressure: monitor heap usage in real time, pause message consumption when it climbs to a high water mark, resume once it drops to a safe level. Messages queue safely in Pub/Sub in the meantime.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); max-width: 65ch;"><strong>The lesson:</strong> crashes went from a recurring operational problem to essentially eliminated. The pattern was reused in other Pub/Sub consumers across the platform. Constraints matter more than code — a pod memory limit is real, and feedback loops (pause/resume) beat throwing resources at the symptom.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Impact -->
    <section style="margin-bottom: 48px;">
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">Impact</h2>

      <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 32px; padding: 32px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);">
        <div style="font-size: var(--fs-56); font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">DAYS → SUB-MINUTE</div>
        <div style="font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 65ch; margin: 0 auto;">From data arriving days late to sub-minute freshness for webhooks, up to 6 hours for custom integrations</div>
      </div>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">Why It Mattered</h3>
        <ul style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Real-time recommendations became possible. Merchants could see recommendations update within seconds of customer actions.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Conversion attribution could link orders to specific blocks and email clicks — what proved to merchants that recommendations were actually working.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Segmentation worked with fresh data. Audiences updated in minutes, not hours.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">Reporting moved off a cost curve that scaled with query volume onto one the team controlled.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 12px;">Scale</h3>
        <ul style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">200+ merchants · 5 platforms · 3-month migration · rollback path remained available and was not used</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">New sources (Klaviyo, Zendesk) plugged in as streaming integrations, not custom pipelines</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">Completed migration off legacy architecture within 3 months with the rollback path available throughout cutover</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What I'd Change Today -->
    <section>
      <h2 style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 16px;">What I'd Change Today</h2>

      <div style="margin-bottom: 24px;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">What I'd Preserve</h3>
        <ul style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">Raw landing layer (reversibility principle held)</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;">CDC at the landing store, not each source, to keep downstream replay and validation centralized</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">Table-per-tenant for isolation (multi-tenant contention is worse than ops cost)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 style="font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px;">What I'd Change</h3>
        <ul style="max-width: 65ch; list-style: none; padding: 0;">
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Datastream → pure Debezium from day one.</strong> Datastream was our transition strategy; we could have earned off it faster. Debezium proved itself in production.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink); margin-bottom: 12px;"><strong>Consider separate CDC per domain.</strong> Commerce CDC vs. click-tracking CDC would reduce blast radius of unplanned events.</li>
          <li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--ink);">​<strong>Evaluate Iceberg for analytics layer.</strong> Wasn't production-ready at the time; would simplify the architecture today.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section style="padding: 52px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); margin-top: 52px;">
      <p style="font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 16px;">Next steps</p>
      <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0;">
        <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">→ <a href="/case-studies/hard-problems" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">See production incidents that shaped this design</a></li>
        <li style="margin-bottom: 12px;">→ <a href="/resume" style="color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none;">Download my resume</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .case-next { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; padding-top: 32px; margin-top: 48px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
</style>
